A||N||5||fastonpumpgas||seized cradle bushings||||
Z||000000||fastonpumpgas||09-10-1999||05:09 PM||||Please help. I dont have any impact, and I cant find anything to cut through the bushing sleave, tried a BFH , the bolt is too rusted .. Any suggestions would be apprecated||||reg||
Z||000001||sluppy123||09-10-1999||11:11 PM||||I had the same problem on one of the bolt's.<BR>I tried using a wrench to turn the bolt in the bushing but it would spring back because of the rubber mount, so I turned it as far as I could and got out the BFH and beat the living hell out of it. I kept this up till it loosened up! ||||reg||4
Z||000002||batboy||09-11-1999||12:19 PM||||I feel your grief. Use lots of Penetrating Oil or WD 40 and big hammer. If you can get some heat onto the bolt without burning up the bushing, that might help too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-11-1999||01:26 PM||||try an impact wrench. Give it a bunch of reall short bursts.||||reg||5
Z||000004||lowCG||09-11-1999||02:11 PM||||Invest in a can of Maltby's penetrating solution,it makes the others seem like water.<BR>On real bad ones,I soak with a squirt a day for about a week before using the wrench,and sometimes to try and tighten it a little,before unturning helps too.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fastonpumpgas||09-11-1999||11:23 PM||||I tried all that, I ended up getting a sawzaw blade for cutting tile, it took about 30 miutes a peice but worked, I was going to buy poly bushings anyway, but becareful, leave the back 2 bolts in, cause the crtadle came down in hurry, thanks any guys.....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
